  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I have this issue on desktop client, where the hair and everything else with dynamic bones is jittering when I move.\nIt looks like my hair moves at 5 fps, stops and then starts moving again. That includes public avatars like Unity-chan and players made.\nI tried a lot of things like changing dynamic bone settings, update rate, copying others settings, but nothing worked. I also reinstalled unity, made my avatar from scratch, tried verifying game integrity, reinstalled the game, went back to older graphic drivers, tried locking the game at 45 and 60 fps, turned on and off vsync, used steam and vrchat account... Nothing worked so far.\n\nI should also mention that people with similar ping to mine (around 130) see no problem with my avatar (EU), but people from NA can easily see it. Now the more I think about this, its starting to look like connection issue, the delay to vrchat servers, but why it doesnt affect others, right?\n\nHere are my PC specs:\n\nIntel Core i5-4590 @3.3 GHz\n\n8GB RAM\n\nWindows 8.1 64 bit\n\nMSI GTX 970 4G GAMING\n\nPS. Heres vide clip recorded in 60 fps\n\nhttps://streamable.com/qs9v6",
